cuems-utils for Debian
======================

The shared Python library of the CUEMS stack, installed as a dh-virtualenv
under /usr/lib/cuems that every other CUEMS package populates. Maintainer
notes (where debian/ lives, how to build, the interpreter check) are in
README.source.

What this package places on a node (feature 011, "/etc/cuems first install")
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  /usr/share/cuems/schemas/*.xsd        the six schemas, package content
  /usr/share/cuems/defaults/*.xml       the three pristine documents, carrying the
                                        reserved sentinel identity (never a real uuid)
  /usr/share/cuems/defaults/system-defaults.toml   the upstream seed values
  /usr/lib/cuems/bin/cuems-init-node    node coherence tool (also /usr/bin/cuems-init-node)

  /etc/cuems/*.xsd                      copied from /usr/share on EVERY configure —
                                        the installed schema always matches the
                                        installed library; never a conffile
  /etc/cuems/{settings,network_map,default_mappings}.xml
                                        created by postinst ONLY WHEN ABSENT, with one
                                        freshly minted uuid4; never modified by the
                                        package afterwards; removed only by purge
  /etc/cuems/defaults.d/*.toml          the operator's site overlay; never shipped,
                                        never touched; applied by cuems-init-node only
  /var/lib/cuems-utils/init-node/       the tool's write record (what it last wrote)

postinst never exits non-zero: this is the base package of the stack and a
failure here would leave every CUEMS package unconfigured. If cuems-init-node
fails or times out, the pristine placeholders are installed, a warning says the
node is NOT PROVISIONED, and `cuems-init-node` provisions it.

Operator commands
-----------------

  cuems-init-node --check       0 coherent · 1 mismatch · 2 absent/unreadable · 3 not provisioned
  cuems-init-node               (re)provision: identity preserved, hand edits kept and reported
  cuems-init-node --reset       back to system defaults (seed values + your overlay), identity kept
  cuems-init-node --force-new-identity --yes   a new uuid; the node must be re-adopted;
                                               then: systemctl restart cuems-nodeconf.service

The Avahi record announcing the node is rendered from /etc/cuems/settings.xml by
cuems-nodeconf at every start and role change; unmask and start it on every
node. Full guide: specs/011-etc-cuems-first-install/migration-guide.md.

